8</issue><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>476</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">McMahon LF Jr, Hayward RA, Saint S, Chernew ME, Fendrick AM. Univariate solutions in a multivariate world; can we afford to practice as in the &#x0201c;good old days&#x0201d;? American Journal of Managed Care. 2005;11(8)473&#x02013;6. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16095433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmittdiel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Vijan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fireman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lafata</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Oestreicher</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Selby</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predicted quality-adjusted life years as a composite measure of the clinical value of diabetes risk factor control</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>2007</year><volume>45</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>321</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.mlr.0000254582.85666.01</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Schmittdiel J, Vijan S, Fireman B, Lafata JE, Oestreicher N, Selby JV. Predicted quality-adjusted life years as a composite measure of the clinical value of diabetes risk factor control. Med Care. 2007;45(4)315&#x02013;21. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17496715</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>